  "intro": "A percent is a part per hundred. Key relationships: part $=$ percent $\\times$ whole, so percent $=\\frac{\\text{part}}{\\text{whole}}$. Percent increase or decrease is $\\frac{\\text{change}}{\\text{original}}\\times 100\\%$. To increase by $r\\%$, multiply by $1+\\frac{r}{100}$; to decrease, multiply by $1-\\frac{r}{100}$. Successive percent changes multiply the factors; they do not add.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "What is $20\\%$ of $150$?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Part $=$ percent $\\times$ whole $=0.20\\times 150$.",
          "Compute: $30$."
        ],
        "answer": "$30$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "A $\\$80$ item is discounted $25\\%$. Find the sale price.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "A $25\\%$ discount keeps $75\\%$: multiply by $0.75$.",
          "$80\\times 0.75=60$.",
          "So the sale price is $\\$60$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\$60$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "A price rises from $\\$40$ to $\\$50$. Find the percent increase.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Change $=50-40=10$.",
          "Percent increase $=\\frac{10}{40}\\times 100\\%$.",
          "That is $25\\%$."
        ],
        "answer": "$25\\%$"
      }
    },
    {
